{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"ec758a4546b1fc90","name":"card_unit_japan_ki_67_peggy","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Homefront/units/card_unit_japan_ki_67_peggy","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"Ki-67 PEGGY","text":"Deployment: Remove an enemy unit that has 3 or less attack.","flavorText":"The Mitsubishi Ki-67 Hiryū, codenamed \"Peggy\" by the Allies, was a twin-engine medium bomber introduced by Japan in 1944. Designed to replace the aging Nakajima Ki-49, the Ki-67 was highly maneuverable and well-armored, a rarity among Japanese aircraft of WWII. It featured self-sealing fuel tanks and could survive significant battle damage, allowing it to dive-bomb and perform low-level escape maneuvers. Powered by two 1,900 hp radial engines, it reached speeds of up to 537 km/h and carried a bomb load of 1,070 kg internally. It was equipped with 12.7 mm and 20 mm defensive guns and saw action across China, Okinawa, French Indochina and the Mariana Islands. A total of 767 units were built, with many deployed against US fleets and airbases in the final stages of the war. Some were modified for suicide missions, including the Sakura-dan variant which carried two 800 kg bombs. Some variants such as night fighters and anti-submarine aircraft were also developed. Its durability and agility made it one of Japan's most capable twin-engine bombers of WWII.","faction":"Japan","type":"bomber","rarity":"Unique","cost":5,"operationCost":2,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_japan_ki_67_peggy","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_japan_ki_67_peggy_title","SourceString":"Ki-67 PEGGY","LocalizedString":"Ki-67 PEGGY"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_japan_ki_67_peggy_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Remove an enemy unit that has 3 or less attack.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: R